  "query_preview": "..\nClear skies and light winds are expected tonight. This may allow \npatchy fog to develop again, mainly in the river valleys. Low will\nbe 20s to low 30s.\n\nThe upper ridge impacting the region will linger into Thursday \nbefore an upper trough pushes in Friday. A weak cold front moves \nin Friday night with a breezy day expected for Saturday. There may\nbe isolated showers around but models are not in agreement with \nplacement and/or timing yet. This front should help to mix the \natmosphere and warm temps above normal starting Friday.\n\nAn upper ridge returns late in the weekend for dry and continued\nmild conditions. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNo major changes were made to the forecast package this afternoon.\nThere is some low to moderate confidence of fog overnight tonight\ninto Wednesday morning again. Otherwise, expect high confidence in\nthe mostly dry and warmer conditions through the week and low\nconfidence in precipitation over the coming weekend.",
